<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Abinova entitlements - deliberately EMPTY.

  Decision (MAC02): Abinova is distributed direct, not through the App
  Store, so the App Sandbox is not enabled.  Sandboxing a document
  editor gains little here and would cost real machinery:

    * opening arbitrary user documents is already fine sandboxed via
      the open dialog, but saving them back needs security-scoped
      bookmarks (per-document, persisted, or the save panel each time);
    * the update check needs com.apple.security.network.client;
    * embedded-object launch and the screenshot path spawn/access
      things the sandbox restricts.

  The hardened runtime (codesign -o runtime, applied by
  dist/sign-macos.sh for Developer-ID signatures) is still used - it
  is what notarization requires and it is independent of the sandbox.

  If a future capability genuinely needs an entitlement (library
  validation exceptions, JIT, ...), add the key inside the dict below -
  sign-macos.sh already passes this file to codesign.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
